+# Final review inv-2, cluster 22 (evidence-hg-lnw-8)
+
+Source: base 60e287aadd08af10779df39e625200f28d4b7fa3, head 985d1eb6faaa2e92e4e01f430f0f2c07618bf6ad (both verified as commits). Caller checkout observed clean at head.
+
+## Scope examined
+
+The cluster is three evidence logs from bead hg-lnw.8 (tier 5 against real threads 3.6.0): evidence/hg-lnw.8/callers.log, tier5.log, tier5-rebased.log. There is no source change in the cluster. I read the slices, the bead acceptance list, the spec's Requirement baseline (B1 to B4, no human scope changes) and the tier-5 tests in tests/threads_real.rs that the logs run.
+
+## Evidence against the bead acceptance list
+
+- tier5.log and tier5-rebased.log: 9 of 9 tests pass in tests/threads_real.rs, exit=0. They include the three window tests (before 24 h, between 24 h and 7 d, after finalization), rebind_places_a_restart_held_seat_on_its_pane, operator_rebind_resurrects_and_places and production_discovery_reaches_real_threads_daemon. The rebased run matches the first run, so the result survived the rebase onto the integration branch.
+- The 24 h to 7 d test asserts a fresh Pending invitation on the seat-wide participation thread (episode 2 after a settled episode 1), which is the tier-5 row added by hg-lnw.15.
+- README line 301 documents the test-support threads build (target/threads-bin-test-support, HG_TEST_THREADS_SUPPORT_BINARY override), so the shortened clocks are reached on a real daemon rather than fake-only.
+- callers.log: adopt_private_herdr 4 of 4 and the threads-binary version-rejection test pass; this covers callers of the changed real-adapter surface.
+- The root_watchdog test passes in each run. No log contains the post-run leak check from AGENTS.md; the logs are plain cargo output, so the "no rig leak" acceptance is not evidenced in this cluster.
+
+## Requirement baseline trace
+
+- B1 (resurrect on undo): the cluster exercises ResurrectSeat through graph's real adapter against a real daemon in all three windows. The production path from undo of a closed tab to the adapter call lies outside this cluster; it is the seam reviewer's to trace.
+- B2 and B4 (frictionless restart, restart-held fresh start): the held-seat rebind test shows the adapter places a held seat on its pane against real threads. The production caller that invokes it before relaunch is outside this cluster; seam reviewer.
+- B3 (v4 session via upstream fix): production_discovery and adopt tests run on a v4 session against the real daemon. The pin and registration code is outside this cluster.
